cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "dinostomp: a validity battery for LLM evaluations"
message: >-
  If you use dinostomp, or reuse its checks, please cite it. When citing a
  RESULT it produced, quote the engine fingerprint alongside the version: the
  version says which release, the fingerprint says which bytes.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kwon
    given-names: Alex
    email: ask@collapseindex.org
    alias: collapseindex
repository-code: "https://github.com/collapseindex/dinostomp"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.39.1
date-released: "2026-08-09"
keywords:
  - evaluation
  - benchmark validity
  - LLM
  - reproducibility
  - contamination
  - LLM-as-judge
  - agent evaluation
abstract: >-
  dinostomp treats every derived evaluation artifact as untrusted and
  re-derives it from the closest available primary evidence. A local-first
  toolkit for building, running and publishing LLM evals, it ships a battery of
  checks over the spec, the dataset, the scorer and every run: scorers must
  demonstrate they can fail before they may score, recorded verdicts are
  re-scored, summaries are recomputed, seeded item selection is re-derived, and
  every input that influences a run (spec, data, scorer, agent, judge, and the
  engine itself) is hashed into the run manifest so post-hoc edits are
  detectable. Checks are split constitutionally: deterministic facts gate,
  statistical inferences only warn. Coverage is reported honestly, so a
  narrowed dataset can never buy a cleaner-looking verdict. The battery is
  validated by an executable scorecard of deliberately defective evals measured
  in both directions, sensitivity and specificity, and several of its checks
  were added or corrected because real models exposed defects in it.
references:
  - type: generic
    title: "DinoTrials: the bad-eval torture suite"
    notes: >-
      The executable scorecard that validates the battery, in trials/. Cite the
      sensitivity and specificity figures together; a battery loud enough to
      catch every planted defect will also flag every innocent pod, and only
      the second arm tells them apart.
